# Staff portal — Vercel deploy (always use this)

When the user asks to **deploy** the employee/staff portal, HIPAA training app, Siya Assist staff shell, or auth API, deploy **both** production projects below (API first, then staff app). Do not use ad-hoc project names.

## Production deploy — local CLI only

**Git/cloud auto-deploy is disabled** for both staff Vercel projects via `ignoreCommand`. Pushes to `main` will **not** promote staff production.

Use only:

```bash
bash scripts/deploy-staff-portal.sh
```

**Dirty-tree gate:** the script prints **branch + commit SHA**, then runs `git status --porcelain`. If anything is dirty, it **exits 1** and prints the listing — it will not deploy. Only an explicit `--allow-dirty` override continues (still prints the dirty list). Use `--check-only` to exercise the gate without promoting.

Do **not** bare-`vercel deploy` the auth API or staff app from the shell — those paths skip this gate. Always use `deploy-staff-portal.sh` so both projects share the same safety check.

Do **not** use Vercel MCP `deploy_to_vercel`, Cursor cloud agent deploy, or bare `vercel deploy --prod` from repo root.

GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/siya-staff-*.yml`) run **CI/QA only** — they never deploy.

## Projects

| Production URL | Vercel project | Source |
|----------------|----------------|--------|
| https://siya-staff-auth-api.vercel.app | `siya-staff-auth-api` | `integrations/hipaa-training-api/` |
| https://siya-staff-assist.vercel.app | `siya-staff-assist` | monorepo root + `vercel.siya-staff-assist.json` |

## Auth API — required path

Deploy **only** from the API package directory (linked project in `integrations/hipaa-training-api/.vercel/`):

```bash
cd integrations/hipaa-training-api && npx vercel deploy --prod --yes
```

**Do not** deploy the auth API with `vercel.hipaa-training-api.json` from the monorepo root — dashboard/build settings there can run the **Next.js staff app** against `siya-staff-auth-api`, breaking `/api/health` and all auth routes.

## Staff app (Next.js)

From repo root:

```bash
cd /Users/sp/amcare-os && npx vercel deploy --prod --yes --project siya-staff-assist --local-config vercel.siya-staff-assist.json
```

## After deploy — smoke check

```bash
curl -sS https://siya-staff-auth-api.vercel.app/api/health
```

Expect JSON with `"ok":true` and `"service":"hipaa-training-api"`. If 404 or HTML, redeploy API from `integrations/hipaa-training-api`.

## Guardrails (permanent)

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `scripts/vercel/should-build-staff-assist.sh` | Skip **all** git builds for `siya-staff-assist` |
| `scripts/vercel/should-build-staff-auth-api.sh` | Skip **all** git builds for `siya-staff-auth-api` |
| `vercel.json` + `vercel.siya-staff-assist.json` | Staff app build + ignoreCommand |
| `integrations/hipaa-training-api/vercel.json` | Auth API ignoreCommand |
| `scripts/deploy-staff-portal.sh` | Canonical prod deploy script |
| `vercel.README.md` | Monorepo deploy map — do not bare-deploy from root |

## Scope

- Do not deploy `siya-assistant` (patient Guide) or `siya-health` unless explicitly requested.
- Do not push git unless the user asked for commit/push.
